    "hardware_bias_mechanism_explanation": "Layer 1 executes in IEEE-754 float32 on the ARM Cortex-A9 CPU where b1_f is added directly every timestep (cur1 = W1 * x + b1_f). Layers 2 and 3 execute on the FPGA event-driven LIF Core Groups (Group 1 and Group 2), which only accumulate 8-bit signed integer (int8) synaptic weights when pre-synaptic spikes arrive and have no dedicated per-timestep bias adder in RTL. To preserve Layer 2 and Layer 3 biases in hardware, Event-Driven Synaptic Bias Folding embeds each neuron's bias into its incoming synaptic weights: W_folded[i, j] = W[i, j] + alpha * b[i], where alpha approximates 1 / (avg_incoming_spikes_per_timestep).",
